@startuml Cross-Reference Routing Sequence
title Cross-Registry Agency Routing -- The Cross-Reference Problem

actor Client
participant "SDMX Proxy" as Proxy
participant "AgencyRoutingService" as Router
database "BIS Registry" as BIS
database "IMF Registry" as IMF

== Step 1: Client fetches BIS DSD with references ==

Client -> Proxy: GET /structure/datastructure/BIS/BIS_DER/1.0\n?references=all\n(no X-Source-Artefact-Urn)

Proxy -> Router: resolveRegistry("BIS", null)
note right of Router
  No URN -> skip cross-ref path
  Standard routing:
    "BIS" in agencies[]
    -> primaryRegistry = "BIS"
    -> found in configs[]
    -> **return BIS**
end note
Router --> Proxy: BIS RegistryConfiguration

Proxy -> BIS: GET /api/v2/structure/datastructure/BIS/BIS_DER/1.0?references=all
BIS --> Proxy: DSD + referenced artefacts

note over Proxy
  Response includes referenced codelist:
  **urn:sdmx:org.sdmx.infomodel.codelist.Codelist=IMF:CL_AREA(1.15)**
  Agency is "IMF" but artefact lives in BIS
end note

Proxy --> Client: DSD + references (including IMF:CL_AREA)

== Step 2: Client fetches the cross-referenced codelist (WITH header) ==

Client -> Proxy: GET /structure/codelist/IMF/CL_AREA/1.15\nX-Source-Artefact-Urn: urn:sdmx:org.sdmx.infomodel\n  .datastructure.DataStructureDefinition=**BIS**:BIS_DER(1.0)

Proxy -> Router: resolveRegistry("IMF",\n"...=BIS:BIS_DER(1.0)")
note right of Router #palegreen
  1. Parse URN -> sourceAgency = "BIS"
  2. Resolve registry for "BIS":
     primaryRegistry = "BIS" -> found
     -> candidateRegistry = **BIS**
  3. Cross-check: is BIS in "IMF"'s registries?
     IMF config: primary="IMF", secondary=["BIS"]
     -> **yes**, BIS is in secondaries
  4. **Return BIS**
end note
Router --> Proxy: BIS RegistryConfiguration

Proxy -> BIS: GET /api/v2/structure/codelist/IMF/CL_AREA/1.15
BIS --> Proxy: Codelist IMF:CL_AREA(1.15)
Proxy --> Client: Codelist (correct!)

== Contrast: WITHOUT header (today's broken behavior) ==

Client -> Proxy: GET /structure/codelist/IMF/CL_AREA/1.15\n(no header)

Proxy -> Router: resolveRegistry("IMF", null)
note right of Router #salmon
  No URN -> skip cross-ref path
  Standard routing:
    "IMF" in agencies[]
    -> primaryRegistry = "IMF"
    -> found in configs[]
    -> **return IMF**
end note
Router --> Proxy: IMF RegistryConfiguration

Proxy -> IMF: GET /api/3.0/structure/codelist/IMF/CL_AREA/1.15
IMF --> Proxy: 404 Not Found (or different version)
Proxy --> Client: Error

== Example: cross-check FAILS (candidate not in agency's registries) ==

note over Client
  Hypothetical: source URN points to ESTAT registry,
  but the requested agency "BIS" is not hosted by ESTAT
end note

Client -> Proxy: GET /structure/codelist/BIS/CL_SOMETHING/1.0\nX-Source-Artefact-Urn: ...=ESTAT:SOME_DSD(1.0)

Proxy -> Router: resolveRegistry("BIS",\n"...=ESTAT:SOME_DSD(1.0)")
note right of Router #lightyellow
  1. Parse URN -> sourceAgency = "ESTAT"
  2. Resolve registry for "ESTAT":
     primaryRegistry = null, secondary=["BIS"]
     -> candidateRegistry = **BIS**
  3. Cross-check: is BIS in "BIS"'s registries?
     BIS config: primary="BIS"
     -> **yes**, BIS is the primary
  4. **Return BIS**
  (Cross-check passes because BIS hosts BIS artefacts)
end note
Router --> Proxy: BIS RegistryConfiguration

@enduml
